TEXT 8 -808 Left 7 ;Example with three major sections: \nTransposition of shield\nReactive compensation element at end of line\nEarth Fault
TEXT 4080 -704 Left 2 ;Line compensation
TEXT 1320 -792 Left 7 ;EARTH FAULT!!
TEXT 1224 -392 Left 6 ;You can see that in the short circuit\ncase with earth fault the shield\ntakes parts of the short circuit current
TEXT 4192 -656 Left 7 ;NO LOAD
TEXT -24 -408 Left 2 ;Note: The shield current is dependent of some parameters: \n1) The thickness of the shield (resistance)\n2) The placement of the conductors (horizontal,trefoil)\n3) Solid or not solid shield (resistance)\nThe files from all examples in this folder is (for ilustrating perfect shielding - so for the untransposed case\nthe shield current is as high as the conductor current) \nwith solid thick shield with conductors 1m horizontal distance so the shielding current is at very high level\nFor a real world cable the shield currents would be smaller as in the simulation (Thin shield with higher resistance)\nTo see this you can change Rsh to a higher value or set "fact" parameter to e.g.10 (default 1)\nFor a thin shield see: OILcable_400kV_1200mm2_shielded_2Xgrounded_TrianglePlacement_ThinSolidShield.acp
TEXT 1744 -704 Left 7 ;Shield_current_400kV_1200mm2_Horizontal_Position_1m_thick_shield_5mm
